# Player profiles and player cards

Two new pages for logged-in players. Tests before code (AGENTS.md).

## Decisions

1. Achievements: games post unlocks to the server (`POST /api/achievements`).
2. Profile picture: user uploads a file or picks a preset (both). Server re-encodes with Pillow
   to a 256 px square, stored under `DATA_DIR/avatars/`.
3. Wish list: rich text with links. Create a link with Ctrl-K (Cmd-K on Mac), or select text and
   right-click, like Teams, Word and PowerPoint.
4. Editing: the owner and admins (`ADMINS`) can edit a profile.
5. Player cards: all logged-in players see all cards. Each card shows scores and achievement
   badges. Nav link `/spillere`.
6. Persistence: deferred. Decide later how `DATA_DIR` is kept on Render.

## Open questions

A. Achievements (agreed: 1a, a POST endpoint that games call).

   Tracks and tiers:
   - Each game defines at most 3 tracks. A track is one kind of achievement (e.g. gifts collected).
   - Each track has tiers in increasing order (e.g. 1 present, 10 presents, 25 presents).
   - A higher tier replaces the lower tier on the card. Only the highest reached tier per track is
     shown, so a card never has more than 3 badges per game.
   - Achievement id format: `<game>:<track>:<tier>`, e.g. `snake:gifts:10`.

   API: `POST /api/achievements` with `{achievement_id}`. The server stores the unlock for the
   session user and ignores repeats. The server does not decide tiers; games send the tier they reached.

   Snake tracks (proposed, 3 max; gifts track dropped, it correlates with score):
   - `snake:ghost-cross`: cross your own body while ghosting (see below). Tiers TBD.
   - Two more tracks TBD. Candidates from the existing code: shield saves (`snake:shield`),
     save streak (`snake:lives`). Pick the two to keep, with their tiers.

   Ghost loops (agreed rules):
   - Ghost gives 10 ticks of passing through the body (GHOST_TICKS = 10).
   - A loop is recorded when the head moves into a body cell while ghosting and stays alive.
   - After a loop, the next floor item is always a ghost powerup.
   - The card text hints at coiling without naming the mechanic (done, commit b38aea8).

   Loop tiers (agreed names):
   - Tier 1, one loop: Nidhogg.
   - Tier 2, two loops at once: Ouroboros.
   - Tier 3, three loops at once: Jormungandr (spelling Jörmungandr if the card font supports it).

   Snake tracks (3 max per game). Agreed:
   - Loops: Nidhogg, Ouroboros, Jormungandr (see above).
   - `snake:shield`: most shields held at once. Tiers 3, 6, 10 (agreed).
   - `snake:trim`: trim pickups in one run. Tiers 3, 6, 10 (agreed).
   Measured with the game's rules (2000 simulated runs, simple bot, 20x20 board):
   - Most shields held at once: best run 6. 5 reached by 1.7% of runs; 10 and 20 never.
   - Trims in one run: best run 8. 5 reached by 1.9% of runs; 10 and 20 never.
   With 3, 6, 10 (simulated, 2000 runs, simple bot):
   - Trims: 3 reached by 11.3%, 6 by 0.8%, 10 never.
   - Shields held: 3 reached by 10.6%, 6 by 0.4%, 10 never.
   Open: tier 10 is not reached by the simple bot. Keep it as a skilled-player target, or
   raise powerup supply.
   Trim rule: removes 3 tail segments, never below 5 segments. Score is kept.

   Badges show the name on hover (title) and the snark as tooltip text.

   Existing unlocks: left in localStorage, not migrated (agreed: 2).

B. Wish list storage (agreed: sanitized HTML, allowlisted tags and URL schemes).
   Options considered: Options:
   - a. Store sanitized HTML. Allowlist tags (`a`, `b`, `i`, `u`, `br`, `ul`, `ol`, `li`) and
     `href` schemes (`https`, `http`, `mailto`) in Python with `html.parser`, no new dependency.
   - b. Store Markdown, render with the existing escape helper. Simpler and safer, but users
     don't get Word-style formatting.
   Recommended: a, because the editor is contenteditable and the sanitizer is the trust boundary.

## Achievement texts (draft, dry System AI voice)

Each card: title, one snark line. Tooltip = snark. Title shown on hover.

Each track has 3 tiers, each with its own name and text. Names agreed. Every tier ends with a
REWARD line. Tone escalates: each tier is more impressed than the last.

Loops (snake):
- Tier 1, Nidhogg (1 loop): "You bit your own tail. On purpose. The System AI has opened a file titled 'Hobbies, Concerning.' Somewhere a dragon is taking notes.
  REWARD: One loop you can call your own. Pity it is the only one."
- Tier 2, Ouroboros (2 loops open at once): "Two loops, both open, both crossing. You are eating yourself in stereo, and the System AI is politely hoping you have a plan. It does not think you have a plan. Look at you, forming a circle of pure self-indulgence.
  REWARD: A gold serpent-scale hat. It fits, unfortunately."
- Tier 3, Jormungandr (3 loops open at once): "Three loops. You have wrapped the whole board around yourself like a scarf on a snake that should know better. Midgard is shaking. The gods are gathering. The System AI has stopped talking, which has never happened before. We are in awe. You are the end of days, and it suits you.
  REWARD: The World Serpent's Ring. Wear it and the sea rises to meet you."

Shields held at once (snake):
- Tier 3, Buckler: "Three shields. You collect protection the way other snakes collect regret. The System AI says prepared. The System AI also says hoarder. It is taking bets.
  REWARD: One Buckler, a small round shield with a rune that stings."
- Tier 6, Aegis: "Six shields held at once. Insurance agents across the galaxy have started calling you back, and they are crying. You are no longer a snake. You are a fortress with a bad attitude.
  REWARD: The Aegis, six shields gleaming. Try not to be smug about it."
- Tier 10, Aegishjalmur (the helm of awe, a protective rune): "Ten shields. The System AI has stopped reading the spreadsheet and is simply staring at you, with what can only be called reverence. Nothing can touch you. Nothing dares.
  REWARD: The Helm of Awe. Every wall on the board feels a little less certain of itself."

Trims in one run (snake):
- Tier 3, Snip of the Norns: "Three cuts. Clean, polite, and deeply unnecessary. Your tail did not ask for this and is still in shock. The Norns are watching with very sharp scissors.
  REWARD: The Snip, a pair of ribbon scissors. Decorate responsibly."
- Tier 6, Shears of Atropos (Atropos cuts the thread of life): "Six trims. Your tail is a rumour now. Santa is asking where the ribbon went, and the elves have formed a committee. Atropos leans over your shoulder, impressed, which is terrifying.
  REWARD: The Shears of Atropos. Do not hold them near anything you care about."
- Tier 10, The Last Cut: "Ten trims. The elves will be talking about this haircut for a decade. The Norns have closed their book, Atropos has put down her shears, and the System AI whispers, 'Well. Look at that.' We have no words. We are reverent. We are slightly afraid of you.
  REWARD: The Last Cut. Not to be used on anything with a pulse."

